{"id":"[REDACTED]","object":"chat.completion","created":1788232673,"model":"mercury-2","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"**CONCRETE BREAK FOUND**\n\nThe recent test suite `test/mercury-run-ledger.test.js` expects the function `classifyMercuryVerdict` to return the string **`'cannot_verify'`** for several common Mercury outcomes (lines 124‑131, 133‑141).  \n\nHowever, the implementation in `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/run-ledger.js` returns **`'unverified'`** when the reviewer‑panel authority ceiling is `UNVERIFIED` (and for other similar branches).  \n\n**Evidence from the test (expected value)**  \n- `test/mercury-run-ledger.test.js:124` → `expect(...).toBe('cannot_verify');`  \n- `test/mercury-run-ledger.test.js:126` → `expect(...).toBe('cannot_verify');`  \n- `test/mercury-run-ledger.test.js:133` → `expect(...).toBe('cannot_verify');`  \n\n**Evidence from the implementation (actual return)**  \n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/run-ledger.js:295‑300` →  \n\n```js\nif (!authority || authority.ceiling === 'UNVERIFIED') return 'unverified';\nif (authority.ceiling !== 'FULL') return 'unverified';\n```\n\nThus the function returns `'unverified'` for the same situations where the tests now require `'cannot_verify'`. This mismatch causes the test suite to fail, proving a concrete break in the recent changes.","tool_calls":[],"tool_call_id":null},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":20249,"completion_tokens":432,"total_tokens":20681,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4437},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":123}},"warning":null,"reasoning_summary":null}